  "title": "DeepSeek broke GitHub's record with a free Claude Code rival",
  "description": "Comment DEEPSEEK and I'll send you the link.\n\nDeepSeek just broke GitHub's all-time speed record, already past a hundred thousand stars in days. It's called DeepSeek Harness, a free rival to Claude Code. The part companies like Anthropic keep locked behind a paid product, the whole engine that runs an AI agent, DeepSeek just gave away for free. Everything in it is swappable, so you're not renting someone's agent, you're building your own on any model you want.\n\nPeople pay two hundred a month for setups like this. DeepSeek open-sourced it under an MIT license that lets anyone run it, for nothing.\n\n#ai #deepseek #opensource #coding #claudecode",
